1
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:12,960
Brighten up and step away, you'll see.

2
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:28,640
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling.

3
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:35,320
Walking while looking back,
holding Gā-chan's hand.

4
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:42,460
That strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,180 --> 00:00:47,740
So, on the tiles of the arcade street,

6
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:53,560
I tried walking only on the black ones.

7
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,680
Everyone was a child once,

8
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:01,840
but everyone has forgotten.

9
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:05,800
Politicians with their self-important faces,

10
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:09,100
and the blue-rinse aunties
who are such an eyesore.

11
00:01:09,620 --> 00:01:12,100
Come on, turn the corner.

12
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:14,700
That corner.

13
00:01:15,740 --> 00:01:19,900
You can meet everyone, everyone.

14
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:24,520
Over there is Kame-ari.

15
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:27,820
Surely, Kame-ari.

16
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:33,080
Everyone, come to our town.

17
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:34,620
Thank you.

18
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:39,420
Far-off Teraike.

19
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:48,920
Good morning, senior.

20
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:50,880
You're here awfully early today, aren't you?

21
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:53,460
To keep up with our
internationalized society,

22
00:01:53,460 --> 00:01:56,840
I was studying Chinese all night
and ended up greeting the morning.

23
00:01:57,820 --> 00:01:58,640
That's the story, see?

24
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:01,260
Wow, that's amazing, senior!

25
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:03,180
What's so amazing about it?

26
00:02:03,180 --> 00:02:04,860
Mahjong, you idiot. Mahjong!

27
00:02:04,860 --> 00:02:06,060
I see.

28
00:02:06,060 --> 00:02:08,500
Anyway, I'm going to bed. Move aside.

29
00:02:10,260 --> 00:02:12,080
What's this, some kind of future map?

30
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:15,420
This is the planned completion
diagram for the Nakagawa Island Project.

31
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:18,180
International competition
is growing ever fiercer.

32
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:19,920
To come out on top in the 21st century,

33
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:21,500
the Nakagawa Group is now

34
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:23,860
reclaiming a third of Tokyo Bay

35
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:26,140
to consolidate the headquarters
buildings of the entire group.

36
00:02:27,820 --> 00:02:33,420
Yes, as expected of the world-class Nakagawa Konzern.
Their scale is on another level.

37
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:39,440
Of course, each company is connected online,
and also linked overseas via satellite communications and optical fiber

38
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:42,620
to become a global communications
hub accessible from anywhere.

39
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:47,180
Since the buildings will be connected by monorail and elevated walkways,
the group

40
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:51,080
will boost exchange within the group and make work run more smoothly,
apparently.

41
00:02:52,060 --> 00:02:56,480
I see. But commuting there would be inconvenient, wouldn't it?
Odaiba, for one, can currently only be reached

42
00:02:57,820 --> 00:03:06,460
by one route, and that's quite inconvenient.
Don't worry, by the time Nakagawa Island is finished, we'll run a non-stop linear subway from Tokyo, Yokohama,

43
00:03:06,460 --> 00:03:16,200
Chiba, and even from my house. That's amazing.
While you're at it, why not make it reachable from Kameari too?

44
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:19,240
That's a good idea.
I'll pass it along to the project team.

45
00:03:22,340 --> 00:03:24,900
Did you make it just in time after
sprinting all the way from the station?

46
00:03:25,440 --> 00:03:26,920
Morning, Mr. Terai.

47
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:28,240
Morning.

48
00:03:28,700 --> 00:03:31,960
For you to be late, Mr. Terai, when
you always arrive fifteen minutes early.

49
00:03:32,740 --> 00:03:34,760
Well, actually, I bought a house.

50
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:36,800
Today was my first day at work, so...

51
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:42,340
That house you mean, is it about that time two years
ago when the real estate agent was going on about it?

52
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:46,640
Yes, after that I looked at all sorts of
properties and finally made up my mind.

53
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:49,440
I thought you'd given up on it, though.

54
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:53,280
Searching for two whole years...
you're a tenacious man.

55
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:55,580
Well, that's only natural
when you're house hunting.

56
00:03:56,780 --> 00:03:57,600
Chief.

57
00:03:58,080 --> 00:03:59,060
Good morning.

58
00:03:59,060 --> 00:04:00,260
Morning.

59
00:04:00,580 --> 00:04:04,000
Ryotsu, when it comes to house hunting,
you must be careful, then even more careful,

60
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,300
and it's instinct to keep
searching until you're satisfied.

61
00:04:06,300 --> 00:04:08,240
You're not buying a model kit,

62
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:11,420
you can't decide lightly,
or you'll end up regretting it later.

63
00:04:11,420 --> 00:04:13,560
You don't have to bring
me into this as an example.

64
00:04:14,340 --> 00:04:17,560
So, Terai, where exactly is your new house?

65
00:04:18,020 --> 00:04:22,200
Well, while I was looking for a cheap place,
I kept going further and further inland.

66
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:24,240
It's probably Chiba or Saitama, right?

67
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:26,240
Because the budget was...

68
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:28,740
So where is it? Just say it clearly!

69
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:33,160
You probably won't know it,
but the nearest station is Kokkyōga-oka.

70
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:36,280
Kokkyōga-oka? I've never even
heard of a station by that name.

71
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:38,720
Is that definitely in Japan?

72
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:41,860
How rude! It's within a perfectly
reasonable commuting distance.

73
00:04:43,560 --> 00:04:44,680
That was really close, wasn't it.

74
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:47,180
It's just that I got a little carried away.

75
00:04:47,180 --> 00:04:49,200
It takes three and a half hours.

76
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:50,820
Three and a half hours?

77
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:53,900
But the lot is 220 tsubo.

78
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:55,880
And each family member has their own room.

79
00:04:55,880 --> 00:04:58,000
And the living room alone is 20 tatami mats.

80
00:04:58,360 --> 00:05:00,140
Well, that's a mansion, isn't it?

81
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:03,280
If you like,
come by on my day off next time.

82
00:05:03,280 --> 00:05:04,400
Please come, all of you.

83
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:05,740
We'll welcome you.

84
00:05:05,740 --> 00:05:07,620
We get free meals!

85
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:08,920
Yeah, that's right.

86
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:11,660
If we go for a drive,
let's all drop in on you.

87
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:15,859
A car won't work, though.

88
00:05:15,909 --> 00:05:18,620
There are some spots along
the way we can't get through.

89
00:05:19,880 --> 00:05:23,280
It's fine! The train runs there.
I'll draw you a map now.

90
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:26,220
If you get lost on the way,
you won't be able to get back, you know.

91
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:29,600
You're not living in the Fuji Sea of Trees,
are you?

92
00:05:36,060 --> 00:05:39,040
They still run steam locomotives out here.

93
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:40,920
It really puts you in the mood, doesn't it?

94
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:44,380
It reminds me of the French countryside.

95
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:47,520
Senpai, how much longer do we have to ride?

96
00:05:47,980 --> 00:05:49,000
Hold on a second.

97
00:05:49,460 --> 00:05:52,400
The station we just passed
was Saihate-ga-oka, so

98
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:54,600
the next one should be Kokkyōga-oka, right?

99
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:56,900
From there we transfer to the single-track line,
and it's the third stop.

100
00:05:56,900 --> 00:05:59,600
I see, so it's no wonder it
takes three and a half hours.

101
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:02,420
Well, he did say the land
was 500 yen per tsubo.

102
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:04,900
500 yen?

103
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:06,520
I bought 200 tsubo.

104
00:06:06,520 --> 00:06:09,000
I was going to buy 200 tsubo,
and apparently 20 tsubo came along with it.

105
00:06:09,420 --> 00:06:11,220
So that makes 220 tsubo, then.

106
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:15,100
What kind of real estate
agent did he buy from?

107
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:19,060
We're here, we're here!

108
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:21,780
This station's so small,
you could mistake it for a restroom.

109
00:06:21,780 --> 00:06:23,900
Still, what an amazing place this is.

110
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:26,780
They said it's in front of the station,
but there isn't even a convenience store.

111
00:06:26,780 --> 00:06:28,260
There isn't a single one, is there?

112
00:06:29,620 --> 00:06:32,460
There should be a bus stop in
front of the station, though.

113
00:06:33,420 --> 00:06:35,280
Senpai, isn't that it over there?

114
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:38,060
Oof.

115
00:06:38,580 --> 00:06:41,440
These are some wild animal's footprints.

116
00:06:41,440 --> 00:06:42,960
What time is the next bus?

117
00:06:42,960 --> 00:06:45,600
Let's see, it's 1:05 now, so...

118
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:48,060
it's about two hours from now.

119
00:06:48,060 --> 00:06:49,720
We have to wait two whole hours?

120
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:52,180
I'm starting to regret coming here.

121
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:03,620
Fancy a Mofutan bus
still running these days.

122
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:06,540
That's more impressive
than the bus in *Totoro*.

123
00:07:07,660 --> 00:07:09,020
Never mind that, look over there.

124
00:07:10,620 --> 00:07:12,340
There's a used car center!

125
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:14,560
That's a pretty big used car center.

126
00:07:15,200 --> 00:07:17,780
How can a business even survive
out in the sticks like this?

127
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:20,460
I wonder why it has names
and addresses written on it.

128
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,700
Chief, thank you all for coming!

129
00:07:24,700 --> 00:07:27,360
Terai, did you buy it from Maitoma?

130
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:30,620
You can't get by around here without a car.

131
00:07:30,620 --> 00:07:32,780
Alright, everyone, hop in.

132
00:07:34,820 --> 00:07:37,980
Since you're at it, you could've
come to pick us up at the station.

133
00:07:41,940 --> 00:07:45,260
Even going shopping at the
supermarket takes thirty minutes by car.

134
00:07:45,260 --> 00:07:47,480
The nearest bus stop is an hour away.

135
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:51,340
It's not one car per household anymore,
it's one car per person.

136
00:07:52,540 --> 00:07:54,100
It's really far, isn't it.

137
00:07:55,240 --> 00:07:59,240
Is that the car with the name on it that was at the bus stop,
the one used for commuting?

138
00:07:59,640 --> 00:08:01,640
There's no way you could
manage it by bicycle.

139
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:04,220
We use them.

140
00:08:08,060 --> 00:08:10,660
Then why not just drive to the station?

141
00:08:11,580 --> 00:08:13,000
The station is a real hassle.

142
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:15,080
And gas money adds up, too.

143
00:08:15,080 --> 00:08:17,680
There's a major used car center here,

144
00:08:17,680 --> 00:08:19,700
where you can buy one
for as little as 5,000 yen.

145
00:08:19,700 --> 00:08:21,920
Why is it so cheap?

146
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:23,340
That's about the same as a bicycle.

147
00:08:23,340 --> 00:08:26,300
Exactly, so these days around the bus stops,

148
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:27,840
it's not abandoned bicycles,

149
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:30,980
but abandoned cars that have
become a pollution problem.

150
00:08:30,980 --> 00:08:32,920
That's worse than Tokyo.

151
00:08:34,620 --> 00:08:35,180
Aaaaaah!

152
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:46,400
We're here! This is it. What a spacious, great house.
The perfect environment for raising kids, right?

153
00:08:47,900 --> 00:08:55,700
Yeah, the greenery and the fresh air are great.
I'm embarrassed. Its only selling point is that it's big, really.

154
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:59,620
The surroundings are wide open too. It feels
like being all alone in the Pacific Ocean.

155
00:09:00,840 --> 00:09:01,960
Well, come on in.

156
00:09:03,060 --> 00:09:04,200
Excuse us.

157
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:06,920
What's this?

158
00:09:06,920 --> 00:09:09,680
It's the transfer timetable.

159
00:09:09,680 --> 00:09:13,100
If we miss one bus,
I might have to invest in a bus line.

160
00:09:13,100 --> 00:09:14,200
Invest.

161
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:16,060
Right this way.

162
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:20,480
Lovely.

163
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:21,940
Riroriga-ru

164
00:09:21,940 --> 00:09:24,780
No wonder you were bragging,
it's quite elaborate.

165
00:09:27,120 --> 00:09:29,180
It's spacious and calm, isn't it.

166
00:09:29,180 --> 00:09:31,340
I decided on it because
I liked this place too.

167
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:33,980
Please, have a seat.

168
00:09:35,080 --> 00:09:38,300
So Terai has become the
master of his own castle now.

169
00:09:38,300 --> 00:09:39,640
That's really something.

170
00:09:39,640 --> 00:09:42,920
Well, from now on it's loans and living together,
you know.

171
00:09:44,540 --> 00:09:47,760
Thank you for coming all this way,
sorry for the trouble.

172
00:09:47,760 --> 00:09:50,500
That's exactly the
right word for this place.

173
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:51,740
Ryo-chan

174
00:09:52,100 --> 00:09:54,180
Hello, ma'am. Sorry for intruding.

175
00:09:55,700 --> 00:09:57,440
This is a housewarming gift from all of us.

176
00:09:58,280 --> 00:10:01,160
You didn't have to go to all this trouble.

177
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:05,500
See, that's why I told you not to bother,
so I came empty-handed.

178
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:07,820
Hey, don't say unnecessary things.

179
00:10:07,820 --> 00:10:09,460
You didn't have to hit me, though.

180
00:10:09,460 --> 00:10:11,920
Here, have some tea.

181
00:10:12,540 --> 00:10:12,900
Hello.

182
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:15,900
Are these your kids? Hello.

183
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:19,400
They look just like Terai,
especially the younger one.

184
00:10:19,400 --> 00:10:21,000
I'm Eitarō, the older brother.

185
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,620
I'm Misaki, the younger sister.

186
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:23,460
Hello.

187
00:10:23,460 --> 00:10:23,700
Hello.

188
00:10:24,220 --> 00:10:26,820
How do your kids get to school?

189
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:28,520
Do you drive them, then?

190
00:10:28,940 --> 00:10:31,940
The elementary school is close.
It's a ten-minute walk.

191
00:10:33,760 --> 00:10:35,980
Hey, kids,
want to play baseball in the yard?

192
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:36,600
Yeah.

193
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:38,240
Alright, let's go!

194
00:10:40,780 --> 00:10:43,840
Ryotsu,
playing with kids is what you're best at.

195
00:10:46,820 --> 00:10:49,220
Sorry, sorry, I'll get serious next time.

196
00:10:51,860 --> 00:10:52,680
Found it!

197
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:57,040
The yard's kind of small,
but the surroundings are way too big.

198
00:10:57,700 --> 00:10:59,940
How about we play at the
elementary school grounds?

199
00:11:01,300 --> 00:11:02,400
At the schoolyard?

200
00:11:03,100 --> 00:11:04,700
It's a ten-minute walk, right?

201
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:06,240
Yeah, but...

202
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:08,660
I don't think that's a good idea.

203
00:11:08,660 --> 00:11:11,080
What are you talking about?
Come on, let's go!

204
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:18,360
So that's the elementary school?

205
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:20,760
It's closer than I thought

206
00:11:21,940 --> 00:11:24,680
Ryo-san, you'd better grab the rope soon.

207
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:26,880
A slope like this is nothing.

208
00:11:28,780 --> 00:11:30,480
It's quite a steep slope

209
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:32,480
What is this slope?

210
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:44,560
Are you okay, Ryo-san?

211
00:11:45,760 --> 00:11:47,040
Ow

212
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:49,860
I told you we should've avoided it.

213
00:11:49,860 --> 00:11:51,920
Sure, the trip there only takes ten minutes,

214
00:11:51,920 --> 00:11:55,280
but with this slope,
the way back takes a whole hour.

215
00:11:55,280 --> 00:11:59,300
Terai, that idiot,
moving to such a godforsaken place!

216
00:12:15,540 --> 00:12:16,860
That's strange, isn't it?

217
00:12:16,860 --> 00:12:18,920
But we already paid this month's share.

218
00:12:19,720 --> 00:12:20,780
What's the matter?

219
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:24,360
It's about the taxes,
but they've come to collect twice.

220
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:26,840
We should have paid the property tax too.

221
00:12:27,300 --> 00:12:29,360
Apparently the collection clerk came again.

222
00:12:30,080 --> 00:12:32,560
Alright, I'll ask the clerk for you.

223
00:12:32,920 --> 00:12:33,920
Excuse me, sir.

224
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:35,760
Always smiling, always cheerful tax payment!

225
00:12:35,760 --> 00:12:37,720
I'm the tax collector
in charge of this area.

226
00:12:38,300 --> 00:12:39,960
I'm not the master of the house, you know.

227
00:12:40,700 --> 00:12:44,400
Your wife definitely says she paid.
Here's the receipt.

228
00:12:44,580 --> 00:12:45,540
Let me take a look.

229
00:12:47,060 --> 00:12:50,740
This part belongs to the neighboring prefecture.
Your share is still unpaid.

230
00:12:51,080 --> 00:12:53,180
What? What's that supposed to mean?

231
00:12:53,640 --> 00:12:55,220
Let me explain with a map.

232
00:12:56,440 --> 00:12:59,140
This district was built by
reclaiming land from a river,

233
00:12:59,190 --> 00:13:00,840
so the river forms the prefectural border.

234
00:13:01,640 --> 00:13:04,060
This house falls right on the border.

235
00:13:04,540 --> 00:13:06,902
Fifty-two percent is in our prefecture,

236
00:13:06,952 --> 00:13:09,180
and forty-eight percent is in the other one.

237
00:13:10,700 --> 00:13:10,860
See?

238
00:13:11,220 --> 00:13:13,000
Shall I tell you the specifics?

239
00:13:14,780 --> 00:13:16,300
This part is set up like this, you see...

240
00:13:21,100 --> 00:13:23,060
So this is how it's divided.

241
00:13:25,260 --> 00:13:28,260
The children's room falls
entirely within our prefecture.

242
00:13:30,140 --> 00:13:33,520
And the bedroom is divided like this.

243
00:13:34,240 --> 00:13:37,800
By the way, does the husband sleep on
the right side of the bed, or the left?

244
00:13:38,200 --> 00:13:38,920
The right.

245
00:13:40,700 --> 00:13:44,900
So the husband sleeps in the neighboring prefecture,
and the wife sleeps in ours. I see.

246
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:46,840
What is this?

247
00:13:51,180 --> 00:14:03,480
The kitchen, toilet, bathroom, upstairs children's room, half the bedroom, and one-third of the current living room are in our prefecture.
Two-thirds of the current living room, the other half of the bedroom, and the guest room belong to the other prefecture.

248
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:06,780
So the phone bill goes
to the other prefecture.

249
00:14:07,160 --> 00:14:10,160
Please pay the gas and
water bills on our side.

250
00:14:10,160 --> 00:14:11,900
Chief, what should we do?

251
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:15,180
We should contact the real
estate agent right away.

252
00:14:16,040 --> 00:14:17,440
Whoa, what's going on?

253
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:20,320
That was close. I almost hit him!

254
00:14:21,140 --> 00:14:23,780
Sorry, I mistook him for a gorilla.

255
00:14:23,780 --> 00:14:26,060
I never expected there to be a person here.

256
00:14:26,060 --> 00:14:27,960
Until last year, this was a field.

257
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:29,180
What's wrong, Ryotsu?

258
00:14:29,180 --> 00:14:30,480
Are you okay, Ryo-chan?

259
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:33,520
I nearly got a posthumous double promotion!

260
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:37,480
The real estate agent said
this area is in Kinryō Ward.

261
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:39,420
That's strange, Tore-tore.

262
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:41,640
It really is in Kinryō Ward.

263
00:14:41,640 --> 00:14:43,620
Watch where you're going, seriously.

264
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:46,300
Since Kinryō Ward is in
the neighboring prefecture...

265
00:14:46,300 --> 00:14:48,060
then it's fine as long as it's on this side.

266
00:14:48,060 --> 00:14:49,660
Hey John, come over here!

267
00:14:53,980 --> 00:14:54,800
Isn't this bad?

268
00:15:00,860 --> 00:15:04,240
Enough already!
This is a goldfish-scooping machine!

269
00:15:04,600 --> 00:15:06,240
Ugh, ugh, ugh, ugh!

270
00:15:06,580 --> 00:15:07,340
You bastard!

271
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:11,120
I thought this was the perfect spot!

272
00:15:11,260 --> 00:15:12,620
Jinka stood up!

273
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:14,500
Hey, hold on a second!

274
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:14,940
Stop it!

275
00:15:16,680 --> 00:15:17,500
Stop it!

276
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:21,240
Honestly, what a place.

277
00:15:23,900 --> 00:15:25,780
That's the real estate agency's car.

278
00:15:25,980 --> 00:15:26,320
What?

279
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:26,440
What?

280
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:29,140
How do you like it, customer?

281
00:15:29,260 --> 00:15:30,960
Isn't the environment wonderful?

282
00:15:31,060 --> 00:15:33,720
This land is, believe it or not,
500 yen per tsubo.

283
00:15:34,320 --> 00:15:35,580
Hey! Real estate agent!

284
00:15:36,080 --> 00:15:36,620
Gulp!

285
00:15:37,420 --> 00:15:40,420
Haven't I seen you somewhere?

286
00:15:40,420 --> 00:15:41,780
W-what are you talking about?

287
00:15:41,920 --> 00:15:44,640
I'm Hata from Nikoniko Real Estate.

288
00:15:44,640 --> 00:15:46,340
I've never even seen you before.

289
00:15:47,880 --> 00:15:49,620
I've got it! You're the one!

290
00:15:49,760 --> 00:15:50,240
Grr!

291
00:15:50,580 --> 00:15:51,460
Eek!

292
00:15:51,980 --> 00:15:54,680
It's you,
Hanyu from Hinjike Real Estate, isn't it!

293
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:57,400
So you were in disguise?

294
00:15:57,840 --> 00:15:58,760
Hey, Hanyu!

295
00:15:58,760 --> 00:16:00,340
How could you tell so many lies?

296
00:16:00,340 --> 00:16:01,820
You made Terai buy that house, didn't you?

297
00:16:01,820 --> 00:16:03,860
Please stop, that's a terrible thing to say!

298
00:16:03,860 --> 00:16:04,480
Shut up!

299
00:16:04,480 --> 00:16:06,660
On that messy plot of land
straddling the prefectural border,

300
00:16:06,660 --> 00:16:08,160
isn't everything around it Kinryō Ward?

301
00:16:08,160 --> 00:16:09,980
Didn't I mention that?

302
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:12,380
I didn't hear a single word about that!

303
00:16:13,060 --> 00:16:15,180
But the contract's already concluded, so

304
00:16:15,180 --> 00:16:16,820
even if you complain afterward,

305
00:16:16,820 --> 00:16:17,200
Shut up!

306
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:18,680
The hunter went and fired his gun

307
00:16:18,680 --> 00:16:20,340
and we nearly got killed!

308
00:16:20,340 --> 00:16:22,380
Hey, make sure no stray bullets reach us!

309
00:16:22,380 --> 00:16:24,340
Give us another thousand
tsubo of land around the house!

310
00:16:24,720 --> 00:16:25,800
That's unreasonable!

311
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:27,293
Then,

312
00:16:27,343 --> 00:16:30,620
Hey, customer!
This guy here, Hanyu is his name...

313
00:16:30,620 --> 00:16:33,720
Stop, please! Fine!
I'll add the thousand tsubo!

314
00:16:33,900 --> 00:16:35,100
Nothing! It's nothing, really!

315
00:16:35,420 --> 00:16:37,000
Lucky you, Mr. Terai.

316
00:16:37,380 --> 00:16:41,080
With a thousand tsubo of land around you,
you won't have to fear hunters anymore.

317
00:16:41,460 --> 00:16:41,800
Yeah.

318
00:16:43,060 --> 00:16:44,800
Wait a second.

319
00:16:45,340 --> 00:16:47,060
Hey! Come here a minute.

320
00:16:49,700 --> 00:16:53,260
They say he sold it claiming the
elementary school was a ten-minute walk away

321
00:16:53,260 --> 00:16:53,660
Gulp!

322
00:16:53,780 --> 00:16:55,120
It's that steep slope.

323
00:16:55,170 --> 00:16:58,179
Sure, the trip there takes ten minutes,
but the way back takes an hour.

324
00:16:58,229 --> 00:16:59,620
That's fraud, isn't it?

325
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:00,040
Gulp!

326
00:17:00,160 --> 00:17:03,580
And on top of that, he apparently claimed
a subway line would open in two years.

327
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:03,940
Gulp, gulp!

328
00:17:04,360 --> 00:17:06,140
That's fraud too, isn't it?

329
00:17:06,300 --> 00:17:07,840
Sir! This guy here is...!

330
00:17:08,120 --> 00:17:09,800
Please don't interfere with my business!

331
00:17:10,420 --> 00:17:11,840
Well, I'm not a monster, you know.

332
00:17:11,890 --> 00:17:15,100
Sell me another 1,000 tsubo,
and I'll let this slide.

333
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:19,040
If you're buying, I don't mind if
it's 1,000 tsubo or 2,000 tsubo.

334
00:17:19,040 --> 00:17:21,969
Good, then I'll buy 2,000
tsubo at one yen each.

335
00:17:22,019 --> 00:17:23,360
Hey, cash.

336
00:17:23,460 --> 00:17:24,440
W-what? That's ridiculous.

337
00:17:25,100 --> 00:17:25,980
If you don't want to, that's fine.

338
00:17:26,360 --> 00:17:27,940
Hey there, Mr. Customer!

339
00:17:27,940 --> 00:17:30,120
Alright, alright. I'll sell, I'll sell.

340
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:33,560
Good. Now I'll let you
make a profit from the rest.

341
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:35,220
Nakagawa, come here for a second!

342
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:37,900
What is it, senpai?

343
00:17:38,280 --> 00:17:40,188
It's the Nakagawa Island plan, but -

344
00:17:40,238 --> 00:17:42,360
Forget Tokyo Bay. Do it here.

345
00:17:43,860 --> 00:17:47,280
If we move the entire Nakagawa
Group to this Kokkyō-ga-oka,

346
00:17:47,330 --> 00:17:50,800
we can transform this backwater
into a great city. Do it!

347
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:52,660
You can't just say something
like that all of a sudden!

348
00:17:52,800 --> 00:17:54,370
Rather than reclaiming Tokyo Bay,

349
00:17:54,420 --> 00:17:58,200
using this land at 500 yen
per tsubo will be far cheaper!

350
00:17:59,320 --> 00:18:00,620
B-but...

351
00:18:00,620 --> 00:18:03,547
Suddenly saying something like that.
Ryo-chan,

352
00:18:03,597 --> 00:18:06,440
you're not up to something strange again,
are you?

353
00:18:06,640 --> 00:18:08,438
Don't be ridiculous. I'm just -

354
00:18:08,488 --> 00:18:11,680
I'm saying this out of concern
for my colleague Terai's happiness.

355
00:18:13,560 --> 00:18:15,560
If the Nakagawa Group moves here,

356
00:18:15,560 --> 00:18:18,900
Nakagawa Railway is
bound to build a new line,

357
00:18:18,900 --> 00:18:21,520
and transportation will
improve dramatically too.

358
00:18:22,100 --> 00:18:23,340
Well, I suppose that's likely.

359
00:18:23,340 --> 00:18:26,880
If that happens, the three-and-a-half-hour
commute will be eliminated,

360
00:18:26,880 --> 00:18:29,800
and plenty of supermarkets and convenience stores will be built,
making life easier.

361
00:18:29,800 --> 00:18:32,460
The children won't have to
take that dangerous slope,

362
00:18:32,460 --> 00:18:34,880
and they'll be able to come home
from elementary school safely.

363
00:18:36,080 --> 00:18:36,440
I see.

364
00:18:36,440 --> 00:18:38,260
Nakagawa, make it so.

365
00:18:38,260 --> 00:18:40,520
Even if you say so, I understand.

366
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:43,660
But I can't change the
plan on my own authority.

367
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:49,120
Senior, please make a simulation that can
persuade the Nakagawa Group's executives.

368
00:18:50,340 --> 00:18:52,240
Leave it to me.

369
00:18:55,740 --> 00:18:59,060
Ryo-chan has been off ever since.
I wonder what happened to him.

370
00:18:59,060 --> 00:19:00,880
Good morning.

371
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:06,120
Ryo, you've been absent without leave for three days.
What on earth have you been doing?

372
00:19:06,840 --> 00:19:08,260
It's the simulation.

373
00:19:08,640 --> 00:19:09,660
You...

374
00:19:10,520 --> 00:19:17,240
Well, I made some pretty amazing CG, so take a look.
Everyone, put these on... what is this?

375
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:26,660
It's set up so you can go inside the CG and tour it in virtual reality.
Virtual reality, I said, virtual reality.

376
00:19:26,660 --> 00:19:29,340
You can have a simulated experience. Kon!

377
00:19:29,880 --> 00:19:31,240
Just put them on.

378
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:39,480
Well, let's go.

379
00:19:42,440 --> 00:19:44,220
This is Kameari Station!

380
00:19:44,220 --> 00:19:48,620
What's going on? Kameari Station
shouldn't have a Platform Zero.

381
00:19:49,040 --> 00:19:51,480
We had the Nakagawa Railway
start running trains through here.

382
00:19:52,460 --> 00:19:54,460
Wow, isn't this a linear motor car?

383
00:19:54,460 --> 00:19:58,560
It reaches 600 km/h, so we can get
to Kokkyō-ga-oka in five minutes.

384
00:19:58,560 --> 00:20:00,040
Come on, get on, get on.

385
00:20:05,220 --> 00:20:06,240
W-wow, that's fast.

386
00:20:11,720 --> 00:20:13,080
The station name has changed.

387
00:20:13,560 --> 00:20:15,460
Kokkyō-ga-oka sounds too lame, so...

388
00:20:15,460 --> 00:20:19,060
We parodied Beverly Hills
and changed it to Kokkyō Hills.

389
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:22,280
A monorail connects to the area
around Terai's house, but...

390
00:20:22,280 --> 00:20:23,640
We're going by helicopter.

391
00:20:26,040 --> 00:20:29,000
This virtual reality thing is really well made,
isn't it?

392
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:30,660
It's virtual reality.

393
00:20:31,380 --> 00:20:31,880
What's that?

394
00:20:32,280 --> 00:20:34,580
Those are the Nagakawa
Group's office buildings.

395
00:20:36,480 --> 00:20:37,920
That's my house.

396
00:20:37,920 --> 00:20:40,980
Your house is right in
front of the monorail station,

397
00:20:40,980 --> 00:20:44,340
so your commute to Kameari
takes less than 30 minutes.

398
00:20:44,800 --> 00:20:46,540
You can cut three hours off it.

399
00:20:46,540 --> 00:20:48,200
That's great, Terai-san.

400
00:20:48,200 --> 00:20:51,740
But with the rice paddies and woods gone,
environmentally speaking,

401
00:20:51,740 --> 00:20:53,700
What, are you saying something extravagant?

402
00:20:53,700 --> 00:20:55,860
Being in front of the station
of such an amazing city means

403
00:20:55,860 --> 00:20:58,120
the land price should
naturally be rising too.

404
00:20:58,120 --> 00:20:59,100
Well, that's true, but

405
00:20:59,560 --> 00:21:01,500
one tsubo is worth 3 million yen, you know.

406
00:21:01,500 --> 00:21:02,860
3 million?

407
00:21:03,040 --> 00:21:06,160
Add the 1,000 tsubo I took
from Hanyu to your land,

408
00:21:06,160 --> 00:21:10,440
and it's 1,220 tsubo,
so it comes to 3.66 billion yen.

409
00:21:11,080 --> 00:21:12,240
W-what, that much?

410
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:13,520
And look here.

411
00:21:13,520 --> 00:21:16,760
To the department stores, banks,
schools, hospitals, and so on,

412
00:21:16,760 --> 00:21:18,940
they're all connected by elevated walkways.

413
00:21:18,940 --> 00:21:20,080
You don't even need a car.

414
00:21:22,020 --> 00:21:23,760
What an amazing era we live in.

415
00:21:23,760 --> 00:21:27,380
With this, you won't even get wet in the rain
going between the buildings,

416
00:21:27,380 --> 00:21:28,860
and you can come and go freely.

417
00:21:29,100 --> 00:21:32,540
Well, let's go check out the observation deck
of the Nakagawa Group headquarters building.

418
00:21:38,860 --> 00:21:40,080
There's even a factory.

419
00:21:41,200 --> 00:21:44,200
The Nakagawa Group gets a lot of overseas guests,
after all.

420
00:21:44,660 --> 00:21:47,400
With this,
I think the executives will approve too.

421
00:21:47,960 --> 00:21:49,720
I'm starting to want to move here myself.

422
00:21:50,200 --> 00:21:53,740
But then it'd feel like living in the city.

423
00:21:54,300 --> 00:21:58,260
Don't be so picky. I'm making things convenient for you,
you know.

424
00:22:01,480 --> 00:22:04,820
Ryotsu, what's that cluster
of facilities at the stadium?

425
00:22:04,980 --> 00:22:07,160
No, that's in the meantime...

426
00:22:17,200 --> 00:22:18,820
Aren't they all gambling halls?

427
00:22:18,820 --> 00:22:21,780
Of course,
we need recreational facilities too.

428
00:22:21,780 --> 00:22:25,060
Are you building this town
to suit your own tastes?

429
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:27,940
Of course not, that's silly.

430
00:22:29,100 --> 00:22:31,180
There's an Edge Zone right
next to the stadium, too.

431
00:22:31,180 --> 00:22:31,480
What?

432
00:22:34,060 --> 00:22:36,740
And why is our police box in there too?

433
00:22:37,560 --> 00:22:41,700
Well, I figured it'd be more
fun if we moved over here too.

434
00:22:41,700 --> 00:22:43,040
You idiot!

435
00:22:43,040 --> 00:22:45,720
What on earth are you thinking?

436
00:22:45,720 --> 00:22:47,820
It's far too harmful an
environment for children.

437
00:22:48,800 --> 00:22:50,900
You go there once in a while too, don't you?

438
00:22:51,520 --> 00:22:53,380
I'm devoted to my wife only.

439
00:22:54,260 --> 00:22:56,820
The gambling halls, the Edge Zone,
and the police box were all just a joke.

440
00:22:56,820 --> 00:22:58,300
I'll delete them later.

441
00:22:59,980 --> 00:23:02,260
Senpai, what's that?

442
00:23:03,300 --> 00:23:04,860
W-what was it again?

443
00:23:06,100 --> 00:23:09,420
It's strange that the prime land in
the middle of town is just vacant.

444
00:23:10,240 --> 00:23:10,600
Hello.

445
00:23:11,840 --> 00:23:15,740
Mr. Ryotsu, I've brought the land contract,
so please sign and stamp it.

446
00:23:16,260 --> 00:23:17,860
Land contract?

447
00:23:18,300 --> 00:23:21,800
You bought 2,000 tsubo for one yen!

448
00:23:21,800 --> 00:23:23,560
Idiot! Don't say unnecessary things!

449
00:23:23,840 --> 00:23:24,800
Just kidding!

450
00:23:27,240 --> 00:23:29,640
That vacant lot is your land, isn't it?

451
00:23:29,640 --> 00:23:31,700
What's that supposed to mean?

452
00:23:31,700 --> 00:23:33,700
That's harsh, Ryo-san.

453
00:23:33,700 --> 00:23:37,300
I refuse to go along with
such a selfish relocation plan.

454
00:23:37,300 --> 00:23:41,800
No way! I poured my entire
fortune into making this CD!

455
00:23:41,800 --> 00:23:45,000
Shut up, you...

456
00:23:45,860 --> 00:23:47,940
Hey, wait, you idiot!

457
00:23:47,940 --> 00:23:50,700
What the hell are you thinking?

458
00:23:50,700 --> 00:23:55,180
Damn it, I thought I'd hit the jackpot!

459
00:23:56,460 --> 00:23:58,720
After all, people have to live honest,
steady lives.

460
00:24:04,400 --> 00:24:06,300
Ugh, why am I so irritated?

461
00:24:06,300 --> 00:24:08,620
I'm so damn angry I can't stand it!

462
00:24:08,620 --> 00:24:11,100
What, you're saying I'm short on calcium?

463
00:24:11,100 --> 00:24:13,240
Shut up, mind your own business!

464
00:24:14,100 --> 00:24:15,680
Ugh, I'm getting annoyed again.

465
00:24:16,060 --> 00:24:18,340
Next time, just tough it out with calcium.

466
00:24:18,800 --> 00:24:19,300
See you around.

